    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's theoretical, but the \"repeatable physical mechanism\" could be the way the algos are programmed to optimize for patterns. if my cognitive rhythm is hitting the exact same frequency as the pattern recognition loops in the execution engine, aren't they essentially interacting with the same signal? it feels less like me \"changing\" the hardware and more like me becoming a part of the same algorithmic synchronization loop. like, if the machine is looking for a pattern and i'm providing that pattern through my focus, how is that not a functional interaction?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
